    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Redmond Property are delighted to present to the market No 15 Milford, Malahide, a bright and spacious three-bedroom semi-detached home perfectly positioned off Yellow Walls Road, adjacent the scenic Broadmeadow Estuary. The property is tastefully decorated and has been meticulously maintained throughout. Extending to approximately 120 sq.m., a particular highlight is the large open plan kitchen extension, which creates a spacious and welcoming heart to the home. This generous living area is ideal for everyday family use and entertaining.\r\n\r\nThis attractive property is ideally positioned close to Malahide village, with its excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and essential services and amenities on your doorstep. The area is renowned for its beautiful coastline, scenic walks and vibrant village atmosphere, while excellent transport links provide easy access to Dublin City and surrounding areas via bus and train.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation offers well-proportioned living spaces designed for modern family life, with a welcoming atmosphere throughout. The bright interior, comfortable reception areas and well-appointed bedrooms create a home that is both practical and inviting.\r\n\r\nWith Malahide Castle and its extensive parklands nearby, together with the Estuary, coastline and Marina all within walking distance, as is Malahide Dart station. No 15 Milford presents an excellent opportunity to enjoy the very best of village and coastal living.\r\n\r\nA wonderful home in an exceptional Malahide location — ideal for those seeking convenience, lifestyle and long-term appeal. Viewing is highly recommended \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION (Ground Floor)\r\n(Please refer to floor plan for individual room measurements)\r\n\r\nHall - Hardwood door, solid oak floor, with guest w.c. / w.h.b. wood floor, bathroom cabinet, under stairs storage press, coving, broadband connection, radiator cover, wall panelling \r\n\r\nLiving room – feature custom built fireplace, shelving oak floor, dado rail, coving, centrepiece, tv point, double doors leading to:- \r\n\r\nOpen plan kitchen / dining room- Excellent range of built in wall and floor units, American style fridge freezer, double oven, electric hob, extractor fan, breakfast bar with built in storage presses,  t.v. point, recessed spotlights, double glazed sliding patio door to rear garden\r\n\r\nUtility room – worktop, tiled splash back, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, Ideal energy efficient boiler installed in December 2024  \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION (First Floor)\r\n\r\nBathroom – w.c., w.h.b., bath, oak floor, power shower, partly tiled walls, skylight, shelving. \r\n\r\nLanding – wall panelling, hot press with foam insulated cylinder \r\n\r\nBedroom (1) Front – Main bedroom with bay window, built in wardrobes with mirror inset, shelving, t.v. point. En-suite with w.c., w.h.b., pumped power shower, wall panelling, mirror \r\n\r\nBedroom (2) Rear - views of Malahide Estuary, excellent range of built in wardrobes with shelving, ladder providing access to attic storage room, floored with Velux windows, panelled walls and ceiling, fitted storage units. \r\n\r\nBedroom (3) Rear - views of Malahide Estuary, fitted wardrobe, shelving \r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\n\r\nOff street parking with cobble lock driveway with room for 2-3 cars outside lights and socket\r\n\r\nLandscaped Rear Garden, south facing, not overlooked with views of the estuary, water feature decking, paved patio area, outside tap, workshop, shed with bar! Extensive lighting, side entrance with gate, wide variety of mature trees, plants and shrubs  \r\n\r\nFEATURES\r\n\r\nWell sought after residential development\r\nQuiet cul-de-sac location\r\nPhonewatch Alarm system\r\nSpacious living accommodation\r\nTastefully decorated throughout\r\nLarge open plan kitchen extension\r\nQuality flooring throughout\r\nNatural gas central heating\r\nSough facing rear garden with shed, not overlooked\r\nAttic storage room\r\nWall panneling in hall and landing\r\nGuest w.c., and main bedroom en-suite\r\nAdjacent Malahide Estuary with views\r\n\r\nVIEWING\r\nBy appointment with Redmond Property Swords\r\nContact Philip Mahon MIPAV"
      },
